{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>My covenant</b> — I cut a covenant with him, for because he offers my sacrifices, life and peace shall come to Israel." "And the sense of <b>and I placed them over Israel</b> — that HaShem gave them to him so that they fear him, and he fears HaShem." "<b>נחת הוא</b> — from the nif'al binyan, and the full form is ננחת, like לב נשבר ונדכה, from the paradigm תראה, תחת, and the sense is doubled [a merism]. And some say: <b>and I placed them for him</b> — commandments and statutes, and they are the Torah of priests."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:11.747009879Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}